camchrome: --cc-no-farble also turns off 988's WebGL readPixels perturbation.

220 made --cc-no-farble switch off every per-site perturbation (canvas 2D readback, toDataURL,
measureText, the per-site GPU pick). 988 added a readPixels pass afterwards that was gated only on
--disable-fingerprint-noise, so with --cc-no-farble a WebGL coordinate gradient still read back
perturbed pixels (detected by checkers as "WebGL readback noise"). It now honours the switch.

Tests: tools/network_selftest.py no-farble-switch checks 2D canvas and WebGL readPixels.
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
index 12f236ba25..f44cfcad9c 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
@@ -6160,7 +6160,10 @@
     return;
   const base::CommandLine* command_line =
       base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
+  // camchrome: --cc-no-farble (220) turns every per-site perturbation off; this readback pass
+  // (988) was the one path that still applied it.
   if (!command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kFingerprint) ||
+      command_line->HasSwitch("cc-no-farble") ||
       !ungoogled::FingerprintNoiseEnabled() ||
       ungoogled::CurrentPersona().webgl_real) {
     return;
